Which license applies to what you run
-------------------------------------

Non-commercial (Gaussian-Splatting License), because the code compiles or
imports files derived from SOF, StopThePop, CoMe or GOF:
  - the GOFish renderer extension (threedgut_tracer/src, built by
    threedgut_tracer/setup_3dgut.py), which every GOFish render uses: training,
    render.py with every --renderer (exact, exact-forward, realtime) and
    threedgrut.benchmark.  It includes SOF's hierarchical sort
    (sofMid8Hierarchy.inl, sofMid8Schedule.inl, sofMaximumResponseDepth.cuh) and
    the SOF/CoMe paths of gutKBufferRenderer.cuh, rayPayload*.cuh,
    shRadiativeGaussianParticles.cuh and splatRaster.cpp;
  - training, train.py (threedgrut/trainer.py: SOF and CoMe losses);
  - mesh extraction, mesh.py (gofish/mesh/, GOF and SOF; its extension
    includes opacityField.cuh);
  - the ScanNet++ mesh evaluator.
So training, rendering and meshing GOFish, and the paper pipeline as a whole,
are for non-commercial research and evaluation only.

Without Gaussian-Splatting-License code (they neither import nor compile the files above;
GOFish's own files CC BY-NC 4.0, NVIDIA-derived files Apache-2.0):
  - gofish_ppisp/ (PPISP with the Wide-Angle Appearance Modeling factors,
    gofish_ppisp/wide_angle.py) and gofish/appearance/;
  - the Calibrated Mip Filtering components threedgrut/physical_mip.py with
    threedgrut/physical_mip_csrc/, threedgut_tracer/view_observation_filter.py
    and the footprint operator (footprint_shape_operator*);
  - the camera-domain and calibration-table tools (gofish/camera/,
    threedgut_tracer/kb_table/, gofish/tools/), dataset preparation (gofish/data/),
    and the FIORD, FullCircle, ScanNet++ rendering and T&T rendering evaluators;
  - the T&T geometry evaluator runs the MIT Tanks and Temples toolbox.

